WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:05.680
Writing can seem like an impossible task when
you're learning English.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:10.519
The good news is that with a bit of practice,
you’ll be writing with ease in no time.

00:00:10.519 --> 00:00:14.000
Let’s take a look at different ways to improve
your writing.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.200
This may sound a bit strange, but read as 
much as you can.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:24.760
You’ll be amazed at how many writing tips
you can pick up by simply reading.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:29.000
You’ll pick up the writing tone, different
styles and new phrases,

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.000
all of which will help you.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.870
Next, try writing and ask someone to read
what you’ve written.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:44.010
I know feedback can be tough sometimes, but
finding out if you're getting your ideas across

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:47.059
is an important step in improving your writing.

00:00:47.059 --> 00:00:52.200
It can be scary at first, but can be the most
rewarding bit of the writing process.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.700
Ask a friend, teacher or classmate for their
feedback.

00:00:57.129 --> 00:00:58.980
Did they understand your text?

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:00.430
Did they enjoy it?

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:03.999
This can help you understand what worked and
what didn’t.

00:01:03.999 --> 00:01:08.300
Don’t take it personally, and focus on what
needs improving.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.000
You don’t always have to write long pieces
of text to improve your writing.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.280
With all the social media platforms out there,
you could try microblogging or getting involved

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:24.740
in forums and chats in areas you're 
interested in.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:30.430
If you are organising a book club, you could
also write down your thoughts before you go.

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:34.330
Another easy way to practise your writing
is to keep a diary.

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:37.810
It can be as simple as writing down what you
did during the day.

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:42.000
Or you could treat your diary as a notebook
for ideas to develop later on.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.710
With writing, it’s not about the length
of each text but it's about writing as much

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:51.950
as you can in as many different situations
as possible.

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:54.800
With a few minutes of consistent practice
every day,

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.230
you will gain confidence in no time.

